From: pdx203 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: gpu: per-class ring timeline and a per-process outstanding-job limit

The CP runs the one ring in order, so the render server's composition and scanout copy wait behind every job queued before
them. Framed submissions are tagged with their class (the render server's connection, slot 0, or another process) and the ring
timeline adds, per class, GPU time and the time from the WPTR write to the CP's start stamp (native_adreno_ring_class). A process
other than the render server may have at most native_adreno_app_depth submissions outstanding (0 no limit, the default); past it
its submit is answered kIOReturnBusy and Turnip waits for its own oldest job and submits again.

